From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] controller: synchronize profile on every agent radio

The Topology Response path persisted the validated Multi-AP profile in the
device data model, but the controller radio objects retained the profile with
which they happened to be created.  When a radio was created before the
asynchronous device-profile commit completed, it remained Profile 1 or
reserved.  AP Metrics Responses from the Profile-3 agent were then rejected
because their valid Profile-2/3 TLVs appeared forbidden to that stale radio
object.

After validating the peer's Topology Response profile, apply it to every
controller radio object belonging to that agent as well as to the persistent
device model.  The protocol-reported profile is authoritative and all radios
of one Multi-AP Agent share it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
---
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -2468,6 +2468,17 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_topology_response(unsigned char *buff, unsigned i
 
 	m_peer_profile = profile;
     dm->m_device.m_device_info.profile = profile;
+
+    // A radio object can be created before the asynchronous device-model
+    // commit records the profile.  Keep every runtime radio for this Agent in
+    // sync with the validated profile carried by the Topology Response.
+    std::vector<em_t *> agent_radios;
+    get_mgr()->get_all_em_for_al_mac(src_al_mac, agent_radios);
+    for (auto *radio : agent_radios) {
+        if (radio != nullptr) {
+            radio->set_profile_type(profile);
+        }
+    }
     
 	if (em_msg_t(em_msg_type_topo_resp, m_peer_profile, buff, len).validate(errors) == 0) {
         printf("%s:%d: topology response msg validation failed\n", __func__, __LINE__);
